Feature: Hand launch
  The plane starts in your hand. Hold the throttle above 55 % to throw it, the way you
  would at the field, or press launch.

  Expectation: Throttle up throws the plane
    Holding the throttle above 55 % for a moment throws it.
    Given the aircraft is in hand
    When the throttle is above 55 %
    Then the aircraft is flying

  Expectation: The launch button throws the plane
    Given the aircraft is in hand
    When the pilot presses launch
    Then the aircraft is flying

  Expectation: A crash ends the flight
    Given the aircraft is flying
    When the aircraft hits the ground
    Then the aircraft is crashed

  Expectation: Reset picks the plane back up
    With the throttle still up it would be thrown again straight away, so this is about
    resetting with the throttle down.
    Given the throttle is below 55 %
    When the pilot presses reset
    Then the aircraft is in hand
